11. What is filter() in Stream API?
Answer

filter() is used to select elements that satisfy a given condition.

Syntax
stream.filter(condition)

Example
List<Integer> numbers =
Arrays.asList(1,2,3,4,5,6);

numbers.stream()
       .filter(n -> n%2==0)
       .forEach(System.out::println);

Output
2
4
6

Banking Example

Get active accounts only.

accounts.stream()
        .filter(Account::isActive)
        .toList();

Interview Answer

"filter() is an intermediate operation used to select elements matching a specific condition."

12. What is flatMap()?
Answer

map() returns one object for one input.

flatMap() converts multiple collections into a single stream.

Example
List<List<String>> data =
Arrays.asList(
 Arrays.asList("A","B"),
 Arrays.asList("C","D")
);

data.stream()
    .flatMap(List::stream)
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Output
A
B
C
D

Interview Answer

"flatMap() flattens nested collections into a single stream."

13. What is reduce()?
Answer

reduce() combines stream elements into a single result.

Example
List<Integer> nums =
Arrays.asList(1,2,3,4,5);

int sum = nums.stream()
              .reduce(0, Integer::sum);

System.out.println(sum);

Output
15

Find Maximum
int max =
nums.stream()
    .reduce(Integer.MIN_VALUE,
            Integer::max);

Interview Answer

"reduce() performs aggregation operations such as sum, max, min, or custom calculations."

14. What is Method Reference?
Answer

Method Reference is a short form of Lambda Expression.

Syntax
ClassName::methodName

Lambda
list.forEach(x ->
System.out.println(x));

Method Reference
list.forEach(System.out::println);

Types
Static Method Reference
Instance Method Reference
Constructor Reference

Interview Answer

"Method references provide a concise way of referring to existing methods using the :: operator."

15. What is Optional Class?
Answer

Optional helps avoid NullPointerException.

Without Optional
String name = null;
System.out.println(name.length());

Result
NullPointerException

With Optional
Optional<String> name =
Optional.ofNullable(null);

System.out.println(
name.orElse("Unknown"));

Output
Unknown

Important Methods
isPresent()
get()
orElse()
orElseGet()
orElseThrow()
ifPresent()

Interview Answer

"Optional is a container object used to safely handle null values and reduce NullPointerException."

16. Difference Between orElse() and orElseGet()?
orElse()

Always executes.

Optional.of("Java")
        .orElse(getValue());


Even if value exists.

orElseGet()

Executes only when value is absent.

Optional.of("Java")
        .orElseGet(() -> getValue());

Interview Answer

"orElse() eagerly evaluates the default value, whereas orElseGet() lazily evaluates it only when required."

17. What are Default Methods in Interfaces?
Answer

Default methods allow interfaces to contain implementation.

Example
interface Vehicle {

    default void start() {
        System.out.println("Starting");
    }
}

Implementation
class Car implements Vehicle {
}

Usage
new Car().start();

Output
Starting

Advantage
Backward Compatibility

Interview Answer

"Default methods allow adding method implementations to interfaces without breaking existing classes."

18. What are Static Methods in Interfaces?
Answer

Java 8 allows static methods inside interfaces.

Example
interface Calculator {

    static int add(int a,int b) {
        return a+b;
    }
}

Usage
System.out.println(
Calculator.add(10,20));

Output
30

Interview Answer

"Static methods belong to interfaces and can be called without creating an object."

19. What is New Date and Time API?
Answer

Java 8 introduced the java.time package.

Older APIs:

Date
Calendar


had thread-safety and design issues.

New Classes
LocalDate
LocalTime
LocalDateTime
ZonedDateTime
Period
Duration

Example
LocalDate today =
LocalDate.now();

System.out.println(today);

Output
2026-08-31

Add Days
LocalDate.now()
         .plusDays(10);

Interview Answer

"Java 8 Date-Time API provides immutable, thread-safe, and easy-to-use date handling classes."

20. What are Parallel Streams?
Answer

Parallel Streams execute operations using multiple CPU cores.

Normal Stream
list.stream()

Parallel Stream
list.parallelStream()

Example
List<Integer> nums =
IntStream.rangeClosed(1,100)
         .boxed()
         .toList();

nums.parallelStream()
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Advantages
Better Performance
Parallel Processing
Utilizes Multiple CPU Cores

Disadvantages
Thread Overhead
Order Not Guaranteed
Not Suitable For Small Collections

Interview Answer

"Parallel Streams improve performance by processing data concurrently using the ForkJoinPool framework."

